description: Product copy punctuation. No middle-dot separators or em dashes.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Copy

Do not use middle dots (`·`) as separators. Do not use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) in product copy, errors, labels, or comments we write.

Split into two fields, two sentences, or a comma. Domain names and code (`wedding.pompeii.com`, `foo.bar`) are fine.

```tsx
// BAD
<p>{coupleA} · {coupleB}</p>
<p>This step didn't save — go back or retry.</p>

// GOOD
<Label>You</Label>
<p>{coupleA}</p>
<Label>Your partner</Label>
<p>{coupleB}</p>
<p>This step didn't save, go back or retry.</p>
```
